-- W9 port of test/llvm_fixtures_modules/record_xmod_field_type_collision/entry.mdk
-- (#1418) — the SAME-INDEX, DIFFERENT-FIELD-TYPE spelling of the cross-module
-- record identity defect (#1281/#1382, fixed). Kept distinct from
-- `record_xmod_field_order/`: there the two records disagree about field ORDER,
-- here they agree about order and disagree about the field's TYPE, so what the
-- wrong record buys is the wrong SLOT REPRESENTATION (an unboxed Float cell read
-- as a tagged Int) rather than the wrong offset — genuinely different codegen
-- hazard for a backend to get wrong, worth its own wasm cell.
--
-- This module imports `aaf` — NOT `Cfg` — from `aacfg`, and `Cfg` only from
-- `zzcfg`. `Cfg` at the literal below can therefore only mean zzcfg's, the sole
-- `Cfg` this module ever brings into scope.
--
-- Expected output, derived BY HAND before this fixture was ever run, identically
-- to the already-hand-derived LLVM original: `Cfg { fld = 7 }` then `.fld`, so `7`.
--
-- Live differential (native oracle) gate — no golden to enshrine. Checked against
-- the hand-derived value above, not just against each other.
import aacfg.{aaf}
import zzcfg.{Cfg}

v : Cfg
v = Cfg { fld = 7 }

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (intToString v.fld)
